      "mechanics": "Five own parent/child wrappers use item-source, held-slot, and actual hit_weakspot gates. Four families add 14/16/18/20 percentage points per layer; Recon Lasgun P3 adds 3.5/4/4.5/5 points; cap is five layers. The successful critical-roll event clears without requiring a target hit. In a single processed event batch, the parent adds eligible hit layers before applying the critical clear. Newly added stacks are effective only after the queued event and stat-cache update. There is no independent stack TTL; switching deactivates the held-slot-gated bonus but retains uncleared stacks, while actual unequip removes the source blessing buff.",
      "action_coverage": "All 13 bound marks have ordinary and aimed hit-scan routes. Autogun P3 and Galvanic Rifle P1 special actions are melee stock sweeps and can qualify only if the same-item/held/weakspot event conditions are met. Infantry and Recon Lasgun and Heavy Stubber specials toggle flashlights and do not emit an attack hit. No bound charge or thrown attack route was identified. Full-auto critical cadence follows action state and max_critical_shots rather than an independent roll per projectile.",
      "calculations": "I-tier Infantry Lasgun Kantrael Mk VII (lasgun_p1_m1), action_shoot_hip: with a stated 20% pre-blessing combined roll input, no other modifiers/conversions, five qualifying weakspot hits without a critical, and cache updates between attacks, the fifth attack rolls with four layers and the next with five: clamp(20% + 5×14%, 0%, 100%) = 90%, +70 percentage points / +350% relative to the assumed input. IV-tier Recon Lasgun Accatran Mk XIV (lasgun_p3_m3), action_shoot_hip/full_auto with max_critical_shots=2 and five layers already cached: clamp(20% + 5×5%, 0%, 100%) = 45%, +25 percentage points / +125% relative. These are conditional roll-input examples, not measured weapon baselines or final damage.",
